1785543975966319	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExvBE		item.create	bn-2u01	{"description":"Track A of Phase 7 (bn-1mzi -> bn-2dbp/bn-18y1 -> bn-3ctl) is four risk:high bones whose product value is bounded recovery: open = checkpoint + suffix instead of O(log). Before the formal algebra work starts, measure what checkpoints could actually save on current trunk: (1) read spikes/recovery_scale first — prior scaling data may already exist from the Spike D era; (2) measure LogEngine::open wall time vs corpus size at 2-3 sizes (e.g. 0.5/2/8 GiB) on current trunk; (3) attribute open-time composition — raw log I/O + frame parse vs registry rebuild vs ActiveIndex bulk apply vs payload decode (bn-3hm4 found reopen bulk apply is 18.6% of a 31ms window in the degenerate 1-event shape; what is it in realistic shapes at scale?); (4) note that checkpoints eliminate the prefix scan entirely while effects+suffix eliminates payload decode — so the composition determines which half of Track A carries the value. Deliverable: s/GiB curve, composition table, the implied checkpoint win at stated target log sizes (state assumptions explicitly), and a keep/drop/rescope recommendation for the four Track A bones. mess-bench recovery floor today: 0.12 s/GiB parallel, 0.23 serial (warm cache — state the cold-cache caveat).","kind":"task","title":"Phase 7 premise check: engine-open scaling and composition before the SegmentEffect/checkpoint chain"}	blake3:9c9_VACb7jvsH4x9MhZvOUjkDgj_7WGK-6Jyc_QWVPY
