1785548474954285	mess-pack-adopt	itc:v3:AWKZ_kmfJySZJQAAAAAAQbf6t9dVqgAAAAEvAQ		item.move	bn-3l8n	{"state":"doing"}	blake3:Xhu-jD4vcIj1PFCRK5ZwVh2xvLHNXjBg-cgsCpFtXBw
1785548474960233	mess-pack-adopt	itc:v3:AWKZ_kmfJySZJQAAAAAAQbf6t9dVqgAAAAEvAg		item.assign	bn-3l8n	{"action":"assign","agent":"mess-pack-adopt"}	blake3:oyZhHNnPVoZGO4u1pO_5kCJVPbdbEqM8aBICRi5fO8g
1785548594899130	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAEx0RE		item.comment	bn-bka2	{"body":"Lead review finding addressed — commit d99c9ad8 (workspace bn-bka2, on top of 5706e09c; review cr-377lcv still open).\n\nCONFIRMED and fixed as prescribed (option a). Lazy attach gated the index CRC on FLAG_SPLIT_CRC and left every block entry's `crc` as None for a pre-bn-bka2 sidecar, so such a file attached with NO checksum at all — neither trunk's whole-image `content_crc` at open nor the new per-block CRCs. Since legacy `.pcol`s persist indefinitely on already-sealed immutable segments, that hit every existing store, and it is the exact case the per-block CRC exists to stop (a flipped byte in a raw `dict_id == 0` block can decode into plausible-but-wrong payload bytes). Correctness regression, not a timing shift. Agreed.\n\nFix: `SealedPayloadIndex::attach` reads and parses the 32-byte header FIRST, and when `flags & FLAG_SPLIT_CRC == 0` reads the whole image and returns `from_bytes(bytes)` — `content_crc` verified, bytes resident in the `BlockSource::Memory` variant that already existed. Trunk-identical behaviour for old segments; every seal from here on sets the flag and gets the lazy attach; `archive_reblock` upgrades an old sidecar when it runs.\n\nConsequence worth stating plainly: **the open-time win applies to segments sealed by this build, not to sidecars already on disk.** My 8 GiB / 2 GiB demonstration corpora were built by this build, so those numbers (727.9 -> 13.3 ms, 2417 -> 22.7 MB) describe a store sealed from here on. A store sealed before this change opens exactly as it does on trunk until its segments are re-sealed or archive-reblocked. That is the trade the fix deliberately makes, and it is the right one — an existing store keeps every check it has today.\n\nDocumented as a \"lazy attach requires FLAG_SPLIT_CRC\" rule in four places: the module docs (its own paragraph under the eager/lazy split, plus point 3 of the corruption-timing section), the `open` doc, the `is_resident` doc, and the `SealedSegmentIndex::open` attach-site comment.\n\nNew test `torn_legacy_sidecar_is_dropped_at_open_like_trunk`: build the legacy image first (stripping the split CRCs recomputes `content_crc` over clean bytes, so the file is a valid pre-bn-bka2 sidecar), THEN tear a byte in the DATA region — real after-the-fact media damage that only `content_crc` can see. Open must return `Corrupt(\"content CRC mismatch\")`, i.e. the sidecar is dropped at open and reads degrade to the raw log, byte-for-byte trunk's behaviour. Includes a clean-image control that attaches and serves. `legacy_sidecar_without_split_crcs_attaches_eagerly_and_reads` (renamed) now asserts `is_resident()` with a comment saying why lazily would be wrong.\n\nRe-verified: `cargo nextest run -p mess-index` 145 pass (was 144), 5 skipped; mess-store sealed suites (`engine_block_reads`, `engine_reopen`, `engine_seal_pack`, `cache`) 19 pass, 1 skipped; `cargo check --workspace --all-targets` green; `just fmt-check` clean; clippy unchanged (same 3 pre-existing warnings in pack.rs/driver.rs, none new). Per the lead, the full mess-bench ABBA was NOT re-run — the bench seals in-process with the flag set, so this path is not on the floors' code paths. Workspace left unsynced (still stale vs epoch 3c262ee7) for the lead's rebase at merge; bone stays `doing`, claims held."}	blake3:MZs9D3FPdJLQsuoUdPQJNaksEY0PtIegs0HuJ-UcrIE
1785548697796895	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAEx0hE		item.move	bn-bka2	{"state":"done"}	blake3:YQ34_nauhMSjRJUt1qmUOsFc_al0x-tfLVx8zSjLxqA
1785549789595192	mess-pack-adopt	itc:v3:AWKZ_kmfJySZJQAAAAAAQbf6t9dVqgAAAAEvAw		item.comment	bn-3l8n	{"body":"bn-3l8n done in workspace bn-3l8n, commit f23b7202 (+209d6417 seal events), review cr-6ck986 (NOT self-approved).\n\nSCOPE: per the lead's ruling, deliverable is 'make fjall deletion (bn-fj34) mechanical'. Deferred public API (SnapshotCompatibility/SnapshotCoverage, scan_snapshots cursors, CertifiedSnapshotRef), GC tooling, and the certification/measurement matrices are OUT (framing correction on bn-o5b; deferred API has its own bone).\n\nPATH CONVENTION: app snapshot sidecar = <store>/.snapshots.packs/ (mess_cli::store::snapshot_pack_dir, social::store_backend::snapshot_root). A NEW directory, not the old .snapshots/, so the two layouts never share a root. Old fjall dirs are ignored -- never read, migrated, or deleted; a reopened old store has no sidecar, every load misses, and it replays. Save mode: default Buffered everywhere (matches fjall's journal-buffered head); no consumer here has a durability knob to attach Durable to.\n\nADOPTION MAP\n- examples/social: Store/StoreProjections/open_store/snapshot_root on packs; seed.rs test mod, hot_post_bench, seed_profile (SnapBackend), README, and all rustdoc. --rebuild proof and projection checkpoint untouched.\n- mess-cli: store::snapshot_meta_dir -> store::snapshot_pack_dir; metaread enumerates via Sidecar::open_reader + stream_names/load (no lock, no create/truncate/repair/rename/delete), bounded by published head count. LiveSnapshot shape deliberately UNCHANGED (stream_id stays the interim FNV id) so doctor/inspect/retention JSON is byte-identical. meta-store-locked degradation now applies only to the legacy <dir>/meta source; app snapshots are readable against a live writer. backup.rs documents the sidecar as a deliberate exclusion from the cut (discardable, UUID-scoped, recomputable from the events already in the cut).\n- mess-store: tests/common (TestSnapshotBackend, Reopen, open_snapshot), owned_append, examples/owned_append_bench, lib.rs doc. fjall_snapshot.rs module doc marked superseded ('do not construct in new code').\n- mess-index/src/meta: doc-only note that no live path writes snapshot_stream_names any more. (Did not touch mess-index/src/sealed -- bn-bka2's area.)\n\nGOLDENS (the one place needing a judgement call): tests/golden/v3+v4 are immutable and their tarballs contain a fjall-era store/snapshots/{meta,blobs}. Step 6 became the compatibility assertion the law demands -- the committed sidecar MISSES safely under the pack reader (None, not an error) and the read-only open creates nothing in it (no LOCK, no IDENTITY) -- and the state-blob byte assertion MOVED to step 7, derived from committed payloads via build_cert/take_snapshot rather than read back out of a sidecar, so a state-encoding change still breaks the golden. The generator now writes a pack sidecar, so the next vN pins the new layout positively. Reviewed compatibility statement added to tests/golden/README.md.\n\nEVIDENCE (re-run after maw auto-rebased onto bn-bka2's merge, epoch 29b2326684e4)\n- cargo nextest run -p mess-store, MESS_SNAPSHOT_LAW_ITERS=25: 238 passed, 5 skipped\n- cargo nextest run -p mess-cli: 40 passed, 3 skipped (incl. golden_v3/v4, doctor_app_snapshots, retention_explain, backup_restore)\n- cargo nextest run -p social: 122 passed, 3 skipped (incl. seed_profile_smoke -- bn-2cye's registry-record counts unchanged -- and rebuild::tests::rebuild_matches_after_checkpoint)\n- cargo check --workspace --all-targets: clean; just fmt-check: clean; no new rustdoc warnings\n- Binary --rebuild proof on a real seeded store on packs: PASS (111555 bytes of fingerprint compared). Re-ran with a planted legacy <dir>/.snapshots/meta/marker present: still PASS, marker byte-intact, directory untouched.\n- Seeded store layout confirmed: <dir>/{LOCK,sealed,seg-*.log,.snapshots.packs/{IDENTITY,LOCK,pack-<uuid>-*.open}}\n\nREMAINING FjallSnapshotBackend HITS (all fjall's own impl/tests or docs retiring with bn-fj34): mess-store/src/lib.rs (re-export + one doc line), mess-store/src/fjall_snapshot.rs (the impl), mess-store/src/pack_snapshot/mod.rs:3 (doc naming what it replaces), mess-store/tests/fjall_snapshot.rs (its own suite), mess-store/tests/pack_snapshot.rs (the pack-vs-fjall differential -- deliberately NOT weakened), mess-index/src/meta/mod.rs (3 doc lines).\n\nNOT MIGRATED, deliberately: spikes/** and notes/** name FjallSnapshotBackend in frozen measurement reports and research docs -- historical records, not live paths. docs/adr/0002 likewise."}	blake3:sOt5wJH006gi8v92i6b8XdFLhbNb2T8z_-H_kqM5rWA
