1785603876023177	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAEx6xE		item.link	bn-1w4h	{"link_type":"blocks","target":"bn-11g"}	blake3:1ZyUacrTSKqc6aUT-A6LEKv4cuLeRRyhOBDJdN-9jac
1785604137415844	mess-pack-ident	itc:v3:AWLyczM8nPJkkQAAAAAAQfXbb13rVAAAAAEvAw		item.comment	bn-11g	{"body":"bn-11g implementation complete — workspace .maw/workspaces/bn-11g, commit abeb5e4d, review cr-ph03gs (requested @mess-security, NOT self-approved).\n\n## Spec (normative)\n- docs/spec/01-log-format.md §3.3.1: trailer `flags` bit 0 = SEAL_PACK_IDENTITY (was reserved).\n- docs/spec/01-log-format.md §3.3.2 kind table: kind 3 = SealPackIdentity, 48-byte entry.\n- docs/spec/01-log-format.md **§3.3.3 (new)**: identity bytes, hash domain/version, entry layout, writer rules (1-3), reader rules (1-4), forward/backward compat. Plus **D-FMT-10** (why the footer names it; why the legacy policy; why identity_kind is not advisory-skippable).\n- docs/spec/02-recovery.md §8.3 corrupt-extension Decision: added the SealPackIdentity **exception** — \"treat the extension as absent\" is safe for anchors (rebuild) but is a trust *downgrade* for the identity, so the flag lives under footer_crc and the reader fails closed.\n\n## Encoding\nidentity = blake3(pack header ++ section directory) = the pack's own trailer hash, recomputed+verified by every open. Entry (48 B): identity_kind:u16=1 (SEALPACK_HDRDIR_BLAKE3, a combined domain+version tag) | pack_format_version:u16 | reserved:u32 | segment_id:u64 | identity:[u8;32]. Section emitted FIRST in the region; order is not normative.\n\n## Install ordering (the argument)\nSealDriver::seal_consolidated takes the identity from `SealedSegmentIndex::from_pack` — the verified parse-back of the exact bytes — and calls finalize(Some(id)) only AFTER write_durable_metered returns (temp -> fsync -> rename -> parent dir fsync). Crash between => durable pack, no footer (footerless candidate, scan-confirmed, re-queued). Crash during => torn footer fails footer_crc => unsealed => full scan. The inverse (footer naming absent/partial bytes) is unreachable. FinalizeFn signature changed to FnOnce(Option<PackIdentity>). No second installation record was introduced.\n\n## Validation matrix (footer x pack -> behaviour)\n| names identity | that exact pack | ADMITTED |\n| names identity | different pack, same coverage | REFUTED pack-identity-mismatch |\n| names identity | legacy .pidx stand-in | REFUTED pack-identity-mismatch |\n| names identity | absent | no candidate; cold tier lost, raw log serves |\n| names identity | unparsable | REFUTED unparsable (bn-30u, unchanged) |\n| identity bits corrupt / dup / unknown kind / wrong segment | any | REFUTED pack-identity-unresolvable — never downgraded to coverage-only |\n| names none (legacy) | any parseable pack | ADMITTED on coverage alone (documented D-FMT-10 policy) |\n| absent/torn footer | durable pack | footerless candidate, scan-confirmed, re-queued |\n\nEvery refusal raw-falls-back; all tests re-assert the full read surface byte-exact.\n\n## CLI\nverify: seal-pack-identity-verified (Ok), seal-pack-identity-mismatch / seal-pack-missing / seal-pack-unreadable / seal-pack-identity-unresolvable (Error), seal-pack-unnamed (Warn, the legacy policy). Fields: expected_identity, observed_identity (null when absent), fallback='raw-segment-scan', path, segment_id. inspect: per-segment has_seal + named_seal_pack (hex or null).\n\n## Tests (36 new)\n- mess-log: 8 footer_ext unit (roundtrip, flag+section written together, legacy byte-identical, flipped identity bit breaks ext_crc but not the flag, unknown kind, duplicate sections, malformed section, coexists with anchors) + 4 sealer_suite (named footer reads back real+sim; corrupt extension absent-but-flag-survives real+sim).\n- mess-index: 4 pack (identity == trailer hash; deterministic; stale/copied/extra-section differ; flipped header/dir bit fails the hash) + 3 driver (**named pack durable+verified before finalize runs**, asserted from inside the closure by re-reading and re-deriving; sidecar path names none; reseal of different content differs).\n- mess-store: 12 in tests/seal_pack_identity.rs (every rolled footer names its pack; stale replacement; same-coverage different-content forgery; .pidx stand-in; identity-bit corruption never downgrades; unknown identity_kind; wrong segment_id; legacy footer still admits; sidecar-mode unaffected; torn pack/footer ordering converges; named footer + absent pack; **pack-mode -> sidecar-mode footer shrink keeps the trailer at EOF**) + extended bn-30u's a_corrupt_seal_pack_candidate_takes_the_same_lifecycle with before/after identity assertions (re-seal names the NEW pack).\n- mess-cli: 6 verify surface tests (matching Ok; mismatch expected vs observed + exit != 0; missing pack null observed; corrupt identity reports unresolvable NOT unnamed; legacy = Warn, exit 0; unsealed = silent).\n\n## Gates\n- cargo nextest run -p mess-log -p mess-index -p mess-store -p mess-cli: **788 passed** (was 751), 25 skipped.\n- cargo check --workspace --all-targets: clean.\n- just fmt-check: clean.\n- mess-bench --mode full vs floors.json: **PASS, 14/14 within tolerance**.\n- Did NOT run full `just test` (lead gates).\n\n## Incidental fix found while implementing\nfinalize_footer now set_len()s to exactly content_len + footer.len(). Pre-bn-11g every footer was exactly the 100-byte trailer, so a re-seal overwrote it exactly. A footer can now SHRINK (a pack-mode store re-sealed with seal_pack off), which would leave stale bytes past the trailer and make the segment read as permanently unsealed. Regression test: re_sealing_with_packs_off_leaves_the_trailer_at_eof.\n\n## Notes / deferred\n- mess-log manifest entries gained `flags` in 2 of the 4 reserved per-entry bytes (MANIFEST_VERSION unchanged; old manifests decode flags=0). recover_all's rebuilt entries write flags=0 and ext_len=0 as before — documented, and nothing decides pack trust from a manifest (spec 01 §3.3.3 reads the trailer itself).\n- seal_active (live head) drops the identity deliberately: no footer means no accepted installation record, and inventing a second one is what D-FMT-10 rejects. Its candidate stays scan-confirmed as before.\n- pack.rs territory touched: trailer/identity/open-validation only (PackIdentity type, identity on ParsedPack/PackDirectory, PackHeader.format_version). **encode_pack and the DIRCODEC chooser are untouched** — no overlap with bn-we9x.\n- from_pack(bytes.clone()) in the install path left alone (bn-2t2e).\n- No push, no merge; bone stays doing, claims held."}	blake3:n2eO5GojzWAI5dYILagK-FLHZez1jKB3uGGfkbwpyss
1785604488800027	mess-pack-ident	itc:v3:AWLyczM8nPJkkQAAAAAAQfXbb13rVAAAAAEvBA		item.comment	bn-11g	{"body":"Rebase update: workspace synced onto the current epoch, which had advanced with bn-we9x (dir-codec observability). 3 structured conflicts, all additive on both sides, resolved by keeping both:\n- crates/mess-index/src/sealed/mod.rs — merged the two `pub use pack::{...}` lists (DIRCODEC_*/dircodec_name + PACK_FORMAT_VERSION/PackIdentity).\n- crates/mess-index/src/sealed/segment.rs — SealedSegmentIndex gains both `dir_codec: u16` (bn-we9x) and `pack: Option<(PackIdentity, u16)>` (bn-11g), plus both accessors and all three constructor sites.\n- crates/mess-cli/src/inspect.rs — the segment row carries both `dir_codec` and `has_seal`/`named_seal_pack`; both helper fns kept.\nNo semantic overlap: bn-11g never touches encode_pack or the §12.6 chooser, and the identity does not read or affect codec_id.\n\nPost-rebase re-verification (all on the merged tree):\n- cargo nextest run -p mess-log -p mess-index -p mess-store -p mess-cli: **796 passed**, 25 skipped.\n- cargo check --workspace --all-targets: clean. just fmt-check: clean.\n- mess-bench --mode full vs floors.json: **PASS, 14/14**.\n- maw ws merge bn-11g --into default --check: **[OK] Ready to merge**.\n\nFinal commits: b49c57f7 (feature), b95ddc59 (review metadata), cdaa2946 (conflict resolution), 22983dad (strip maw conflict headers). Review cr-ph03gs still open with @mess-security; bone stays doing, claims held, nothing pushed or merged."}	blake3:lBOaw_4eNfYOQb2WI-DxN7_zRvmHz8KtjGvxznCv1T0
1785604624824836	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAEx7BE		item.move	bn-11g	{"state":"done"}	blake3:KYDtbEyeQ0Jhy9YHDicX2EsAWukkQbQhKmykdlk8ENM
