1785604674915227	mess-cli-seal	itc:v3:AWLyZPnPJ8kzQAAAAAAAQfWvu9fVsAAAAAEsAg		item.assign	bn-1w4h	{"action":"assign","agent":"mess-cli-seal"}	blake3:LRFCZvEil3aU-Z_wLY_qz0lxZvDRKHNmWfwv1uVl-hw
1785605254962691	mess-seal-rss	itc:v3:AWLMkzMnnJJzJlAAAAAAQdq217qu1oAAAAExAw		item.comment	bn-2t2e	{"body":"Implemented in workspace bn-2t2e (.maw/workspaces/bn-2t2e), commit d97d2a2. Review created: cr-1uwdug (NOT self-approved — awaiting reviewer).\n\nChange (crates/mess-index/src/sealed/driver.rs, seal_consolidated):\n  before: let index = SealedSegmentIndex::from_pack(bytes.clone())?; verify; identity = index.pack_identity(); write_durable; finalize(identity); install(index)  <- the eager verification image WAS the installed index\n  after:  let verified = from_pack(bytes.clone())?; verify; identity = verified.pack_identity(); write_durable; drop(bytes); index = match open_pack(&path) { Ok(lazy) if lazy.pack_identity()==identity => {drop(verified); lazy}, _ => verified }; finalize(identity); install(index)\n\nIdentity: still derived from the VERIFIED parse-back of the exact bytes (trailer blake3 recomputed there), never from the buffer and never from the re-open — the re-open must equal it or it is discarded. That makes the footer name one the durable file is now OBSERVED to yield, a check trunk did not make.\nOrdering: unchanged. Pack durable (temp/fsync/rename/dir-fsync) strictly before the footer names it; the re-open sits between the durable write and finalize and only reads. Install-then-evict unchanged. Crash windows unchanged (both fail safe to footerless -> scan-confirm -> re-seal).\n\nAlso adds SealedSegmentIndex::resident_bytes() (size observable next to sections_resident) and test seal_consolidated_installs_the_pack_lazily — asserts !sections_resident, resident_bytes == a fresh open_pack's, and <1/20th of the pack, pinned against open_pack_eager (== pack_len) as the pack-sized reference. Confirmed to FAIL against the old eager install.\n\nEvidence: cargo nextest -p mess-index -p mess-store = 444/444 pass (bn-dbz laziness + bn-30u lifecycle + bn-11g identity suites green); cargo check --workspace --all-targets clean; just fmt-check clean. Residency demo (throwaway, not committed) 16 payload-heavy segments = 32.35 MiB of packs: sum(index.resident_bytes) 33.9 MB -> 1008 B, sections_resident false for all, process RSS delta +76.4 MiB -> +5.9 MiB (13x)."}	blake3:4ne4OWPbwHaCRvHlrSGAVfIZL7vpO5yPKqT0rRD3T4Y
1785605370855494	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAEx7RE		item.move	bn-2t2e	{"state":"done"}	blake3:wIBtn6PRuLFFgctDvhuEe1Odr9Ntq2EHWv2FdPhww3w
1785605838031629	mess-cli-seal	itc:v3:AWLyZPnPJ8kzQAAAAAAAQfWvu9fVsAAAAAEsAw		item.comment	bn-1w4h	{"body":"Implemented in ws bn-1w4h, commit e34e3eb, review cr-1j1s08 (requested from mess-dev, NOT self-approved). Bone stays `doing`; claims held.\n\nSURFACE MAP (before -> after)\n- store::discover_segments / SegmentFile: already carried has_seal (bn-11g) but no classification -> new `SealedArtifact` (Pack|Sidecar|None) mirroring LogEngine::load_sealed's dual read (pack wins; a shadowed .pidx is inert), plus `sealed_artifact_path`, `pidx_shadowed_by_pack`, `discover_seal_packs`, `discover_quarantined` (reuses mess_store::sealed_candidate::{segment_id_from_name, PRIMARY_EXTENSIONS, QUARANTINE_SUFFIX}).\n- doctor: \"sealed but no .pidx sidecar\" for EVERY healthy pack segment -> classification-based; new seal-pack-ok / seal-pack-corrupt / seal-pack-segment-mismatch / pidx-shadowed-by-pack (Info) / quarantined-candidate (Warn, with state=pending-reseal|resealed, parses=bool) / quarantined-sibling (Info) / no-quarantined-artifacts (Ok) + `quarantined` count in the envelope. Pack opened with open_pack (what a reopen would do).\n- verify: pack opened ONLY when a footer named it -> single open_pack_eager feeds both the pack's own trailer-hash/section check (seal-pack-verified / seal-pack-corrupt, new) and bn-11g's identity check (five kinds unchanged, no duplicate findings — corrupt-and-named still reports seal-pack-unreadable only). New orphan-seal-pack sweep; quarantined-candidate at Info.\n- retention: `if !seg.has_pidx { continue }` skipped every pack segment -> both shapes decided by the same decide_segment; row carries `artifact`; a segment whose only candidate is quarantined gets an explicit `quarantined-no-verdict` Info so an absent row is never read as deletable.\n- backup: .seal now rides the cut (see decision below); *.refuted excluded.\n- inspect: per-row `sealed_artifact`, envelope `quarantined` array (always present, empty on a healthy store).\n- rebuild-index: see gaps.\n\nBACKUP POLICY DECISION: the .seal pack RIDES THE CUT, same discardable-vs-cut treatment as the .pidx family, and the reason is stronger than symmetry. bn-11g binds the footer to the exact pack, and the footer lives inside the .log bytes the cut copies whole — so the pre-fix behaviour restored a store whose footer named a pack that did not exist: `mess verify` reports seal-pack-missing (Error) and `mess restore`'s own verify gate FAILS the restore. Backup+restore of a pack-sealed store was broken today, latent only because seal_pack is off. The cut must be identity-complete, not merely data-complete. Excluded and documented inline: *.refuted (source-store evidence + that store's re-seal trigger; copying it imports an anomaly and re-queues a seal the restore just wrote clean), and .par/.reg left exactly as they were — .reg is bn-w5my's call, .par is recomputable from the copied .log and named by no footer, so neither can produce the identity gap .seal did.\n\nGAPS DOCUMENTED (not forced):\n1. `mess rebuild-index` emits the LEGACY sidecar shape only; there is no offline pack encoder. A .pidx rebuilt for a pack-sealed segment is inert at best (dual read prefers the pack) and refutable at worst — when the footer names a SealPack, a legacy .pidx offered in its place is exactly PackIdentityMismatch, so the next open would quarantine the file the command just wrote. Fix: skip pack-sealed segments with a `pack-sealed-segment-skipped` Warn naming re-seal as the remedy; write nothing. A real \"rebuild a pack offline\" needs engine work (expose the pack encoder + the footer identity finalize path) — worth its own bone if operators want it.\n2. The refutation REASON is not durable — bn-30u logs it loudly at the refuting open and the marker carries only the artifact kind. doctor re-derives the one class it honestly can (do the quarantined bytes still parse => `unparsable` vs a coverage/identity refutation) and points at `mess verify` for the exact identity finding. A durable reason would need a marker-side record, i.e. engine work in bn-30u's territory.\n3. Quarantine markers are reported by doctor/verify/inspect and skipped by retention decisions, but nothing in the CLI converges them — that is deliberately the engine's next open. All CLI quarantine handling is read-only and a test asserts the marker bytes survive doctor+verify+inspect+retention byte-identical.\n\nEVIDENCE: mess-cli 69/69 (19 new in tests/seal_namespace.rs, incl. healthy pack store => zero Warn/Error findings; quarantine finding; bn-11g identity mismatch still exactly one finding; engine-rolled background-sealed pack store clean under doctor+verify; backup->restore of a pack store clean and identity-verified) + pack variants added to retention_explain (blocked verdict over a .seal), inspect_report_shape (sealed_artifact per shape), rebuild_byte_equal (pack skip). mess-store 335/335. golden v3/v4 still verify clean. `cargo check --workspace --all-targets` green; `just fmt-check` green. Full `just test` and mess-bench deliberately not run per bone instructions."}	blake3:7mNIssniNovYQARuszH2W8QXMClcCQeyJMIBoaz0Goc
1785605982450271	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAEx7hE		item.move	bn-1w4h	{"state":"done"}	blake3:1dngUhLCtGGwRylU7zAQYeXw7Kxf_HeSSIvdvPMVFpc
1785606024178477	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAEx7xE		item.create	bn-3h64	{"description":"SealPack reserves a REGISTRY_DELTA section and never emits it, so a pack-sealed store keeps the O(#names) registry pread path at open while loose-sidecar stores got bn-26pp's 38.5x cold-open win from .reg files. Phase 8 note on bn-35fy: emit or accept the regression knowingly before defaulting. Emit: seal_consolidated writes the segment's $registry batches into the reserved section (reuse regdelta.rs's encoder — same bytes as a .reg body; section CRC per the pack directory contract). Consume: the engine's sidecar-trusted recover branch, for a pack-sealed segment, reads the section (bounded pread via the directory — bn-dbz's lazy machinery) instead of per-name preads, gated by the same accepts_registry_delta layout cross-check against the pack's own pointer directory. Fallback unchanged: absent/invalid section = pread path, per segment. Differential guard: bn-26pp's registry_delta_differential suite gains a pack-sealed arm proving identical folded registry from section, .reg, and log-only. Target: pack-sealed cold open at high stream counts within noise of the .reg path.","kind":"task","title":"Emit REGISTRY_DELTA in SealPack and consume it at open (close the pack cold-open gap before bn-ccx1)"}	blake3:ThRV8lYwB4lyk6vOFh9oePzECf87g7VSZzZjaTjrkZE
