1785611086339929	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAEx-BE		item.comment	bn-35fy	{"body":"Phase 8 closed 2026-08-01, one session, ten merges. Every named blocker fixed with measured evidence: reopen RSS +1012MB -> +6.6MB at 10M events (bn-dbz) and in-process seal residency 76MB -> 6MB (bn-2t2e); footer binds exact pack identity, fail-closed under extension corruption (bn-11g, plus an incidental shrinking-footer bug); refuted candidates quarantine durably and converge to re-seal (bn-30u); chooser corrected from Spike H's lookup crossover to the exact byte break-even, deterministic (bn-we9x); sealed-directory map on foldhash +47.7% real-corpus lookups (bn-dcr); operator tooling fully pack-aware including a backup->restore identity-completeness break found and fixed pre-flip (bn-1w4h); REGISTRY_DELTA emitted+consumed, pack cold open at parity with .reg (bn-3h64, +0.1% vs 44.9x-slower before). bn-1yor matrix ADMIT: 1136 tests on the pack path, +8.5% buffered under active sealing (~4x fewer seal barriers), 1 file/segment vs 3.88. bn-ccx1 flipped the default with 17 loose-coverage pins and the rebuild-index gap release-noted (bn-3qh0 follows up). Also filed: bn-3odg (active-map foldhash premise), mess-log alloc-count flake noted on ccx1's evidence."}	blake3:cukgJyBCrYx3KbJ1mb88JgFu9jlnpgeTugyWIQ7d4dU
1785611111928611	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAEx-RE		item.create	bn-33l3	{"description":"2026-08-01, during bn-ccx1's workspace suite runs: mess-log::alloc zero_allocs_per_event_on_the_hot_path failed once under full parallel load, passed alone and on a full 1153/1153 re-run. An allocation-COUNT assertion is a mechanism test (good — that is why it exists, bn-31n discipline), but a global allocation counter under a parallel test runner can observe other tests' allocations or allocator pool/arena behavior that only manifests under thread pressure. When it recurs: check whether the counter is process-global vs thread-scoped, whether the assertion window spans a yield point, and whether nextest process-per-test isolation actually applies to this suite (if it is process-isolated, cross-test pollution is impossible and the count is real — then the hot path genuinely allocates under memory pressure and that is a bug, not a flake). One occurrence; filed for the record, do not paper over with a retry.","kind":"bug","title":"flaky: mess-log zero_allocs_per_event_on_the_hot_path fails under parallel suite load (1 occurrence)"}	blake3:f0cMTGYVOxz52_7DaPt5-96n3EA4eNQHrgZ03M9xLos
