1785613364916331	mess-w-1ojm	itc:v3:AWLJySTyTnkzJ0AAAAAAQddVervW1wAAAAEwAw		item.comment	bn-1ojm	{"body":"Started in workspace bn-1ojm: assembling v4 admission dossier. Read spike E REPORT, research 09, ADR 0002 in full, specs 01/04/06, and the bn-11mk and bn-2ctq decisions. Measured gap density on freshly seeded social corpora and verified format constants and read-path behavior in code. Drafting ADR 0003 next."}	blake3:NmcGGWbEGDtHqFYldJikRBx-myNtlXcEi31QcwqJc8k
1785613789148869	mess-w-1ojm	itc:v3:AWLJySTyTnkzJ0AAAAAAQddVervW1wAAAAEwBA		item.comment	bn-1ojm	{"body":"RECOMMENDATION PENDING LEAD RATIFICATION - DECLINE v4. Drafted by mess-w-1ojm 2026-08-01. Record: docs/adr/0003-v4-admission.md. Review: cr-24a8ib (mess-dev requested, not self-approved). Workspace bn-1ojm, 2 commits, not merged.\n\nEVIDENCE (verified against trunk at file and line, not inferred):\n- The constituency is empty. Snapshot install: ADR 0002 lines 363-365, no SnapshotInstalled record in v3 or v4, pack sidecar shipped and default. Projection checkpoints: bn-11mk DECLINE 2026-07-28. Exact dedupe: bn-2ctq DECLINE 2026-07-28. Registry: KEEP v3. Control and event atomicity has nothing admitted to be atomic with, and the one live control does not need it - REG12 already orders a registration strictly before the first domain batch referencing its ids (04-registry.md lines 440-445), and a torn registry batch is never accepted, so the failure mode v4 prevents is already structurally impossible.\n- The gap contract is honored in code, not just prose. engine.rs lines 5055-5077 and 5192 return an exclusive scan frontier; subscription.rs lines 184-220 advance the cursor to max of last delivered plus one and the frontier, and to the frontier alone on a skipped-only page, never to the watermark; stream 0 entries are skipped without a pread at engine.rs 5113 and 5168.\n- v4 frames are strictly larger. v3 is 72 plus 16 equals 88 bytes of framing (format.rs 55 and 116); v4 is 96 plus 32 equals 128 (v4/format.rs 50 and 160). Plus 40 bytes per frame, plus 45.5 percent framing. Neither encoder pads (encode.rs 370-371, v4/capsule.rs 209-213). On the spike bench corpus that is 220 bytes where v3 writes 180, plus 22.2 percent for identical events.\n- The 2 percent scan gate is a per-BYTE gate and by construction cancels that size increase. v4_scan_bench.rs lines 13-18 say so verbatim; the assertion at 157-160 is on per-byte overhead alone. Plus 0.47 percent means the v4 scanner is as efficient per byte as v3, not that a v4 store costs the same to scan.\n- The ADMIT path cannot produce its own evidence right now. bn-3ew9 and bn-31f8 are PUNTED as end-of-project attestation that cannot answer until the engine it certifies exists. Nothing in mess-bench full with floors moves for v4 today because no production path reaches it - mess-store contains zero references to mess_log v4.\n\nMEASUREMENT (gap density, fresh corpora, release build of workspace bn-1ojm at epoch d473744a, social-seed plus mess inspect --format json):\n- social demo, seed 1337: 3,008 global positions, 1,526 domain events, 1,482 registry positions = 49.27 percent gaps.\n- social large, seed 1337: 108,810 positions, 54,602 domain events, 54,208 registry positions = 49.82 percent gaps.\n- Explained by one ratio: gap fraction is about 1 over 1 plus events per stream. Social is stream per aggregate at 1.007 events per stream, which pins it at the maximum of the range. At 10 events per stream it is 9 percent, at 100 it is 1 percent.\n- Framing algebra for a stream receiving E single-event appends: v4 minus v3 equals 40E minus 108 bytes, registry and event payloads cancel. v4 is smaller only below 2.7 appends per stream; at 3 or more it is strictly larger and grows 40 bytes per append forever.\n\nRATIONALE: every named v4 constituency has been individually declined or has no consumer, and format support alone is not product admission (ADR 0002 line 484). The gap problem is contractually solved and costs nothing on the read path. The one cost expressible as a number today - framing - points against v4 for any store whose streams accumulate history. The now-or-never option-value argument is weaker than it looks: bn-2wpj's own scope says mixed v3/v4 detection, fixtures, rollback and downgrade refusal are required EVEN FOR ADOPT-NOW, so adopting now avoids only user-data migration, of which there is none and no 1.0 commitment. And DECLINE does not destroy the option - the tested artifact stays on trunk.\n\nCONSEQUENCES:\n- Closed as conditional work that will not happen: bn-ro0i, bn-5rc6, bn-2wpj, bn-2r8, bn-3ew9, bn-31f8, bn-1zm0. bn-5hcg's exit gate is satisfied by this record.\n- bn-2ctq: the dedupe revisit-under-v4 door CLOSES and its DECLINE becomes standing rather than v3-scoped. Its rationale was encoding-independent - no identified consumer plus free caller-level idempotency via expected-version. v4 addresses exactly one item on its cost list, crash atomicity of key plus events, and none of the others. Making the hard part cheap does not create the consumer. Same escape hatch as everything else.\n- A5 disposition: A5 stands unamended, frame_count at least 1. batch_id remains per-segment and informational only (D-FMT-5). The spike's nonempty-capsule rule plus mandatory batch_id contiguity remains a frozen tested spike capability, not production format; its proof value is preserved in v4_model.rs P1-P7.\n- The v4 module is RETAINED, frozen and demoted, with pointer notes added to lib.rs and v4/mod.rs. 5,219 lines including tests, zero dependents outside mess-log. Recommend retain not delete: it is what makes every reopening path cheap. Deletable later without reopening this decision.\n- Specs reconciled: 01-log-format.md and 04-registry.md no longer present v4 as pending. ADR 0002 section 4 carries a surgical resolved-by pointer; no competing contract remains.\n\nREVISIT IF (any one, each amends ADR 0003 through a fresh gate):\n1. A named consumer for an admitted control whose CORRECTNESS requires atomic commit with domain events. A consumer that only needs a control to exist does not qualify - v3 can carry it as a system record.\n2. A measured composed win outside this host's noise (bn-1gn1 showed 5 percent is inside it), covering the steady state and not only the seeding phase. Requires unpunting bn-31f8.\n3. A real consumer demonstrably harmed by non-dense visible positions in a way the opaque-cursor plus frontier contract cannot fix.\n4. A pre-1.0 decision to make dense visible positions a permanent public promise. This one has a deadline: after 1.0 it becomes a breaking change rather than a format choice.\nAny ADMIT so reached inherits bn-2r8's four gaps as prerequisites.\n\nFINDINGS THAT COMPLICATE THE LANDSCAPE SUMMARY (not suppressed):\na) bn-2r8 says its four gaps are documented in REPORT.md. Only the SIGKILL gap is. The other three trace to the bn-9mw adversarial review, not the report. All four are nonetheless genuine, verified below.\nb) Gap 3 (reserved marker validation) is PARTIALLY closed already: header flags and reserved words are validated at v4/capsule.rs 507-516, but the 32-byte marker's flags and reserved words are written zero at 311 and 315 and never validated on decode (557-565 checks magic and the three echoes only).\nc) Gap 2 is worse than not-written: scanner.rs 763-772 returns a bare None for a non-v3 segment version, indistinguishable from a corrupt or absent header. Safe (no mutation) but not actionable. Latent under DECLINE since no writer emits non-v3.\nd) The gap-density number is 49.8 percent, far above what an aesthetics framing implies. It does not change the verdict - the read path skips those entries without a pread - but it deserved measuring rather than an adjective.\ne) There IS an unlisted v4 constituency the landscape did not name: registration co-commit as a BYTE saving, worth about 21 percent of the social large log. It is an estimate from format constants, not a measurement, and it reverses sign at 3 or more appends per stream. Engaged with in ADR 0003 section 5.2 rather than omitted."}	blake3:A6ShtgrD4GrxhcOhzCRO6QWmiYzEkGPYgArPUOC8SiU
1785614111445402	mess-w-1ojm	itc:v3:AWLJySTyTnkzJ0AAAAAAQddVervW1wAAAAEwBQ		item.comment	bn-1ojm	{"body":"CORRECTION to my RECOMMENDATION comment above (lead review cr-24a8ib, precision finding). That comment states under EVIDENCE point 5: 'mess-store contains zero references to mess_log v4'. That is false in the letter and I am correcting it rather than leaving it in the record. Spike E's two mandatory D4 retry crash tests live at crates/mess-store/tests/v4_d4_retry.rs and reference mess_log v4 six times (lines 24, 25, 26, 27, 166, 232), so mess-store's TEST target links the v4 module. My original grep filtered out tests directories and covered src only.\n\nCorrect statement: crates/mess-store/src contains zero references to mess_log v4 - no production path decodes a capsule, which is what the evidence point actually needed. The single cross-crate dependent is that one spike test, which exercises the RegistryView seam against the real RegistryState and rides the frozen artifact.\n\nConsequence for the retain-don't-delete recommendation: deleting the v4 module later must ALSO remove crates/mess-store/tests/v4_d4_retry.rs in the same change, or mess-store will not build its tests. That is now stated in ADR 0003 rather than left as a trap.\n\nAlso made the 5,219-line figure's scope explicit instead of implied: 2,323 lines mess-log/src/v4 plus 2,295 lines mess-log/tests/v4_*.rs plus 182 lines fuzz_v4_* plus 419 lines mess-store/tests/v4_d4_retry.rs.\n\nFixed in workspace bn-1ojm commit c682c48, across all four sites: ADR section 7 threat notes, the Consequences bullet, the adversarial-analysis row, and the demotion comments in mess-log/src/lib.rs and mess-log/src/v4/mod.rs. No change to the verdict or to any other evidence point."}	blake3:NRC0P693PLYfs6jujP_sld7b1fevttgIMVGK0a2qxsA
1785614194158304	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAEx-hE		item.comment	bn-1ojm	{"body":"DECISION RATIFIED: DECLINE v4. Decided 2026-08-01 (mess-dev, delegated by Bob). Normative record: docs/adr/0003-v4-admission.md, merged at ef02c03c after seal review cr-24a8ib (lead-approved; one precision finding fixed in c682c48c). Verdict basis: the constituency is empty (snapshot install declined by ADR 0002, checkpoints by bn-11mk, dedupe by bn-2ctq, and REG12 already gives the registry crash-safe ordering in v3); the spike scan gate is per-byte and cancels the +40 B/frame framing cost, so a v4 store is bigger and costs more to scan, not less; gap density measured at 49.8 percent on social-large is conceded and answered by the frontier cursor contract, which is honored in code. The dedupe revisit-under-v4 door closes; bn-2ctq DECLINE becomes standing. Four reopening conditions in ADR 0003 section 9. Conditional bones bn-ro0i, bn-5rc6, bn-2wpj, bn-2r8, bn-3ew9, bn-31f8, bn-1zm0 close as work that will not happen."}	blake3:o4rIplwexwITCcEO5628tjL0NaiZVimqtQYcEl1X98c
1785614194187692	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAEx-xE		item.move	bn-1ojm	{"state":"done"}	blake3:MFIZOFsOrrGkTvqjbhsNn8UbTZ1mlqFSIrAzuAfI7IY
