1785696406757191	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExkhI		item.create	bn-3m62	{"description":"Found by bn-3qh0: on a store with seal_pack: true (the default since bn-ccx1), the unsealed live head segment still gets a legacy loose .pidx from the non-pack branch. Footerless, valid, idempotent, superseded when the segment rolls - so harmless, but it means every pack-default store carries exactly one loose sidecar family at all times, which muddies the doctor/verify artifact inventory (bn-11ba reports it as LooseSidecar serving for the head) and the 1.00 files/segment story from bn-1yor. Decide: either the head should get no sealed-index artifact at all until it rolls (check what reads it pre-roll), or the inventory surfaces should classify head-segment sidecars distinctly. Also from bn-3qh0: mess verify reports seal-pack-missing at Error severity for a withdrawn-awaiting-reseal segment; consider whether verify should distinguish owed-reseal (Warn, converges at next open) from genuinely lost (Error).","kind":"task","title":"pack-default stores still write a legacy .pidx for the live head segment"}	blake3:HU34i63fvE-8Q_2QU0fjqDjIne7vQKz7CQmtZYoNAtQ
