1785870316147386	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExqRI		item.comment	bn-1m6c	{"body":"Merged to main at 068dfbe47f9b after lead review. Review cr-3ac27j approved by mess-dev. Verified at source: segment census test asserts more than one sealed segment after cold reopen with on-disk cross-check, engine claim behind the chatter-store config sidecar confirmed at mess-log writer.rs resume which re-allocates the active segment to the opened segment_size, checkpoint discardable law tested for absent and corrupt, SUB2 rules tested both directions, bench profile field honest via debug_assertions. Gates rerun by lead in workspace: check clean, fmt clean, 1323 of 1323 passed. Scroll-back linear-depth finding filed as a separate measurement bone."}	blake3:ko40e-Ia39tCsIds4LkuHrMWMGMuYXkruyRgIGE2IA0
1785870324909930	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExqhI		item.create	bn-e93g	{"description":"Observed during bn-1m6c: the chatter scroll-back pager issues exactly one bounded read_stream call per page (after cursor plus limit), yet page cost is linear in STREAM DEPTH and independent of page size - 122 ms per page on a 1.37M-event channel vs 1.8 ms at 38k events, with a 20-record and a 1000-record page costing the same. Recorded as an open question in examples/chatter README. Hypothesis: read_stream resolves a deep stream position list by walking from the stream start rather than seeking to the after cursor - but the mechanism must be NAMED AT SOURCE before any fix is proposed (which walk dominates: active index chain, sealed per-stream index, pack or pcol resolution, payload fetch). This is a measurement bone per the premise-check discipline: it blocks any construction. Worker brief must demand: reproduce with the chatter corpus at several depths using release builds and the ABBA discipline where comparisons are made, attribute time inside the engine read path at source, Amdahl-bound any proposed improvement against realistic access patterns (how often does anyone page deep history), and end with DROP or PROCEED-with-named-target or RESCOPE. Not yet dispatched.","kind":"task","title":"measure: backward stream paging costs linear in stream depth regardless of page size (chatter scroll-back finding)"}	blake3:iRp0Nq8RRDOpzJHVtbfzX7gMBd5yNvWO1vkZ4DoQMIE
