1785871198819746	sonnet-3ehy	itc:v3:AWKSZPJJyckmZ5QAAAAAQateq66rb0AAAAEyBA		item.comment	bn-3ehy	{"body":"Premise verified in workspace: examples/local_db.rs body is entirely commented out (sqlx/rusqlite migration code, async_std main) with only fn main() {} live. Root Cargo.toml is a virtual manifest; workspace.members lists only examples/bank, examples/chatter, examples/social (plus the crates/ and xtask packages) - no bare examples/local_db.rs target, confirming cargo build --example local_db has never had a target to hit. Grep evidence: grep -rn local_db across the whole tree (excluding .git and target) returns zero hits outside .bones/events/*.events, and those hits are the bones event log recording bn-3jqg discovery comments and this bone creation event about local_db.rs itself - not any code, doc, script, .agents/, justfile, or xtask reference to the file. Nothing actually depends on it. Stub contents before deletion: commented-out use of mess::db::sqlx::migration, sqlx::{migrate::MigrateDatabase, Connection, Sqlite, SqliteConnection}, and tracing_subscriber setup; an async_std::main fn that read DATABASE_URL, created the sqlite db if missing, connected, and ran migration::migrate - a manual local-sqlite-migration smoke tool, superseded by the mess_db test suite and never wired to any package. Preserved here in case anyone goes looking. Action taken: git rm examples/local_db.rs. Gates in workspace: cargo check --workspace --all-targets PASS (clean, no warnings surfaced); just test PASS 1323 passed / 0 failed / 28 skipped; just fmt-check PASS (exit 0, no diff). Workspace epoch: 579ebaa71973 (from main). HEAD after commit: 852cf3aa5e708d4e0b06605b8b5e2fbe29fdc13d, chore: delete dead examples/local_db.rs stub. Seal review cr-12ug6f requested with reviewer mess-dev; not self-approved. Workspace left committed and unmerged."}	blake3:3BIKBbRWbuUMNsgkEjS4Caw38JSAWKuj6Y71Y8PTeAI
