1785885725859841	opus-21ow	itc:v3:AWKSfJP5J5ySTQAAAAAAQavq_q91VgAAAAEvBA		item.comment	bn-21ow	{"body":"DEFECT FOUND WHILE MOVING - reported, NOT fixed (move-only rail). In crates/mess-store/src/engine.rs the doc comment starting \"White-box unit tests for bn-u6o items 1 and 3: LogEngine::run_roll_sealer bounded per-segment wait, and the bounded TOTAL shutdown wait Inner::drop arranges\" is syntactically attached to the declaration mod append_gate_tests, but it describes the OTHER test module, seal_skip_tests, which sat immediately below it. append_gate_tests.rs has its own correct file-level header (Deterministic owner-cohort regression for distinct-stream append overlap) and contains no run_roll_sealer test at all. The misattachment predates this bone and predates bn-2u64 - it is present at 7240a12bc9c2, so some earlier bone inserted the append_gate_tests declaration between the doc and the module it documents. I deliberately left the doc byte-intact where it is and moved only the seal_skip_tests module, because re-attaching a doc comment to a different item is a semantic edit the hard rails forbid. Consequence to be aware of: after this move the doc now sits in engine.rs describing a test module that lives in engine/seal.rs. A one-line follow-up (move those eleven doc lines down to seal_skip_tests in engine/seal.rs) would fix it, but that is a decision for the lead, not a drive-by."}	blake3:AQ8kpL92Vvzok1waYszNwggz-oXfAqivuUEb3-7xhYY
1785885764417389	opus-21ow	itc:v3:AWKSfJP5J5ySTQAAAAAAQavq_q91VgAAAAEvBQ		item.comment	bn-21ow	{"body":"bn-21ow final report 1 of 2 (move-only seam split, part 2 of 3). Workspace bn-21ow, epoch de5daeceb3b251c1914524b14d633a86c6e84496, HEAD e8f67cedc8782697669e8b95665b35b49a343d61, review cr-2hpnx8 (reviewer mess-dev). One commit. Scope check: git status and the staged diff list exactly crates/mess-store/src/engine.rs and crates/mess-store/src/engine/seal.rs, nothing else.\n\nFILE CHOICE. ONE new file, crates/mess-store/src/engine/seal.rs, 508 lines. Two files (seal.rs plus roll.rs) would have split seal_input_from_segment away from one of its two callers and forced a second visibility widening for zero gain, so the whole seal closure is one module. engine.rs drops from 5400 to 4905 lines.\n\nMOVED ITEMS, in the order they appear in seal.rs, all byte-intact including doc comments and their bn citations. One, SealJobGuard (the bn-11ba backlog-gauge guard) with its doc and its Drop impl. Two, a fresh inherent impl LogEngine block holding run_roll_sealer (the background auto-roll sealer loop, bn-1vu / bn-u6o / bn-11ba, with its long doc and its allow(clippy::too_many_arguments)) and then seal_active (the on-demand seal, with its doc). Three, the free fn seal_input_from_segment. Four, the free fn finalize_footer (bn-1vu / bn-11g). Five, cfg(test) mod seal_skip_tests with both of its tests.\n\nTHE EXACT CLOSURE I MAPPED, and what the bone named that turned out NOT to be engine.rs code. The bone listed six things. seal_active, the background sealer and the seal-queue handling including the SealJobGuard interplay, and reseal: all moved (see above), except that the reseal ENQUEUE is not a separate item - it rides the same roll channel and lives inline in open_with (the reseal_tx clone and the resealable loop), which is part 3 territory, so it stayed. Segment roll: there is no roll function in engine.rs - rolling is the committer Roller in mess-log; the only engine-side roll code is the path_for callback and the roll channel wiring, both inline in open_with, part 3. The reg delta emission at seal time: there is NO emission code in engine.rs at all. The .reg sidecar (and the packs REGISTRY_DELTA section) are written entirely by SealDriver in crates/mess-index/src/sealed/driver.rs; engine.rs only CONSUMES a delta, at the RegistryDelta::open(reg_path(...)) site inside recover, which is recovery and therefore part 3. The quarantine and withdrawal call sites: quarantine and withdraw_sealed_index are defined in crates/mess-store/src/sealed_candidate.rs, not engine.rs, and every engine.rs call site that reaches quarantine goes through health.refute inside load_sealed, refute_unparsable, refute_orphans and recover - all open and recovery items, i.e. part 3. withdraw_sealed_index has no engine.rs call site whatsoever; it appears once in an EngineOptions doc comment. Moving any of these would have taken part 3 territory and broken the disjoint-by-file model the split exists to restore, so I left them and am reporting the mapping instead.\n\nLEFT BEHIND ON PURPOSE, under the shared-helper rail. SpinConfig and its Default impl stay in engine.rs: run_roll_sealer takes one, but open_with constructs SpinConfig::default() at the spawn site, so it is shared with code staying behind. It needed NO widening - a child module sees every private item AND every private field of its ancestors, so seal.rs names SpinConfig and reads per_seal_budget and poll_interval with the parent declaration untouched. segment_path stays: eleven call sites across BlockReader, open_with, recover, load_sealed and read_batch_payloads as well as the two seal ones. enumerate_segment_ids stays: shared by seal_active and recover. impl Drop for Inner stays (it joins the seal thread, but it is a trait impl and its subject Inner lives in engine.rs). The whole load_sealed / check_named_pack / refute_unparsable / refute_orphans family stays - part 3. No helper was duplicated and none was relocated.\n\nVISIBILITY WIDENINGS - exactly ONE, forced, minimal. LogEngine::run_roll_sealer goes from fn to pub(super) fn. Forcing use-site: the Self::run_roll_sealer(...) call inside open_with in crates/mess-store/src/engine.rs, in the std::thread::Builder spawn closure that starts the mess-engine-roll-sealer thread - the parent module cannot see a private item of a child module. pub(super) makes it visible in engine and therefore in every engine sibling, which is the minimum. Nothing else on the signature line changed. seal_active was already pub and stayed pub. SealJobGuard, seal_input_from_segment, finalize_footer and seal_skip_tests all stayed exactly as private as they were, because every one of their callers moved with them. NO pub use re-exports were needed: seal_active is an inherent method, which has no module path, and everything else is private with all callers inside the engine subtree."}	blake3:77nBwhID8vKD--K9XZO8gNMbY52UQts9RUsvDcXTBzA
1785885792449059	opus-21ow	itc:v3:AWKSfJP5J5ySTQAAAAAAQavq_q91VgAAAAEvBg		item.comment	bn-21ow	{"body":"bn-21ow final report 2 of 2 - move-only evidence, gates, conventions followed.\n\nMOVE-ONLY EVIDENCE, artefact one: git diff --cached --color-moved=zebra --color-moved-ws=allow-indentation-change over epoch..HEAD, classified by ANSI colour. Totals are 509 insertions and 496 deletions. On the removed side 494 lines are detected as moved and 2 are not; on the added side 493 lines are detected as moved and 16 are not. The one-line asymmetry between 494 and 493 is a blank line that colour-moved paired on the old side but scored as a plain addition on the new side - blanks are below its block-detection threshold - and it is inside the 16 accounted additions below. Every non-move line is accounted for. The 2 plain removals: the old signature line \"fn run_roll_sealer(\" and one blank line that trailed a moved block. The 16 plain additions: \"mod seal;\" (the module declaration), the 8-line module header (7 prose lines plus its bare \"//!\" separator), a blank, \"use super::*;\", a blank, \"impl LogEngine {\", the matching \"}\", the rewritten \"pub(super) fn run_roll_sealer(\", and one blank. That is exactly the allowed set - mod declaration, module header, use statement, impl block wrapper, visibility keyword, blanks - and there were no pub use re-exports to add.\n\nMOVE-ONLY EVIDENCE, artefact two, the multiset check the lead will re-run. The sorted multiset of the 5401 lines of the epoch engine.rs versus the sorted multiset of (HEAD engine.rs, 4906 lines, plus HEAD engine/seal.rs, 509 lines, counting the trailing-newline element) - and I first verified the three engine/ files present at the epoch (append_gate_tests.rs, backend_impl.rs, read.rs) are BYTE-IDENTICAL at HEAD, so they contribute nothing to either side. Result: exactly 1 line appears only in the epoch file, the old \"    fn run_roll_sealer(\" signature; exactly 15 line-instances appear only at HEAD - the 7 header prose lines, one extra bare \"//!\", \"use super::*;\", \"mod seal;\", \"impl LogEngine {\", \"}\", the new \"    pub(super) fn run_roll_sealer(\" signature, and 2 net blank lines. Total delta 16 lines, every one structural, ZERO content lines changed anywhere. (Part 1 delta was 32 lines; this one is 16 because it needed one widening instead of two and one new file instead of two.) No in-body edit, no reordering and no comment reword can be hiding inside a moved block.\n\nGATES. cargo check --workspace --all-targets: clean, zero warnings. just test full suite: 1333 tests run, 1333 passed, 28 skipped - including both soak smokes (soak_smoke_crashless_clean_pass and soak_smoke_survives_crashes_with_all_probes_on), snapshot_law, differential_model, engine_sealed_paging, engine_seal_pack, pack_snapshot, registry_delta_differential and engine_reopen_cycles. Nothing needed a rerun; the soak flake did not appear. just fmt-check: clean on the FIRST try, so there is ZERO formatting churn for the lead to separate from real edits - rustfmt did not reflow a single moved line in its new context (same as part 1).\n\nTWO EXTRA BASELINES, taken unprompted because a module split can shift lints, both by swapping the epoch engine.rs back in and removing seal.rs, then restoring. The cargo clippy -p mess-store --all-targets per-diagnostic set is IDENTICAL between epoch and HEAD (4 diagnostics, same lints, same files, modulo the engine line numbers that necessarily moved). The cargo doc -p mess-store --no-deps per-diagnostic set is IDENTICAL too (18 diagnostics, same set): no intra-doc link broke, and the new module header adds no private-intra-doc-link warning because it uses plain backticks, per part 1 convention three. The tree is clean at HEAD and nothing from those runs is committed.\n\nCONVENTIONS FROM bn-2u64 THAT I FOLLOWED. Rust 2018 layout preserved, engine.rs remains the parent module file, no engine/mod.rs. The mod seal; declaration went into the existing small block right after \"use crate::version::Version\", kept alphabetical: backend_impl, read, seal. The file opens with a short //! header then a blank then \"use super::*;\" and nothing else - that single glob is what makes the move byte-only, and it is why NO widening at all was needed for parent-to-child access (SpinConfig, SealDriver, EngineFs, SegmentSummary, segment_path and the rest are all reached through it). Moved methods went into a fresh inherent impl LogEngine block with untouched bodies. I checked the trait-impl trap FIRST: neither run_roll_sealer nor seal_active is a trait method, both are inherent, so unlike part 1 this split had no forced passengers. The test module moved with the item it tests and became a cfg(test) mod inside seal.rs with its own use super::* (glob of a glob resolves fine, as part 1 documented). Both evidence artefacts produced.\n\nONE DEFECT FOUND AND REPORTED, NOT FIXED - see my preceding comment: the \"White-box unit tests for bn-u6o items 1 and 3\" doc comment in engine.rs is attached to mod append_gate_tests but describes seal_skip_tests. Pre-existing (present at 7240a12bc9c2, before part 1). I left it byte-intact in engine.rs and moved only seal_skip_tests, because re-attaching a doc to a different item is a semantic edit.\n\nI did not push, did not merge, did not run bn done, and did not approve the review. Workspace bn-21ow is committed and unmerged; no claims released."}	blake3:1oljL95t7Dg7ppmdOsSqBRUe3JW3DIBaBQpugLq-H7c
1785901841875149	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExvhI		item.move	bn-21ow	{"state":"done"}	blake3:9JTXZiU9lLmOVHp5lOqv54h-0jxjHZOEaSOvqDCH2Ug
1785901841895369	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExvxI		item.comment	bn-21ow	{"body":"Merged to main at 739356ab4999 after lead review. Move-only proven independently by multiset comparison: 15-line all-structural delta, zero content lines changed, sibling engine files byte-identical. Premise refutation verified at source: the withdraw_sealed_index mention in engine.rs is an intra-doc link, not a call site. Post-merge gates: trunk suite 1333 of 1333, full mess-bench floor gate PASS all 20 within tolerance. The pre-existing misattached bn-u6o doc comment re-attached to seal_skip_tests in a lead chore commit."}	blake3:WAPBIkF-6GxN-G6CAkpanKnZvIvb7VGQN2nUb6Mv3q8
